== B. Rule (fixed before sections A, C, D are computed)
margin = 1/10 = 0.10; min pair fraction = 4/5
derivation: 0.10 = (i) the repo's committed 'material rate' convention (thresholds.py FINAL_ANSWER_MISSING_REVIEW_RATE 0.10; COMMITTED_THRESHOLDS max_tolerated_graph_timeout_rate 0.10); (ii) about the smallest margin a 43-question paired reading can resolve at all (section 1b [computed], cross-checked in section D). Dev cannot set it: section A shows the 10 dev nulls at the ceiling with no discordance. (A first draft of this comment cited a dev null-error rate of 1/10 for drive 2; section A shows 9/9 usable, so that reason was dropped. The value did not change.)
evaluable iff n_pairs >= ceil(0.80 x 43) = 35
  n_pairs=43: guard fails iff net loss b-c >= 5 questions (5/43 = 0.1163 > 0.10)
  n_pairs=40: guard fails iff net loss b-c >= 5 questions (5/40 = 0.1250 > 0.10)
  n_pairs=35: guard fails iff net loss b-c >= 4 questions (4/35 = 0.1143 > 0.10)
  one null question = 2.33 points

== A. Dev evidence (drives 1, 1b, 2; the same 10 dev null questions; D-129: dev only)
dev null questions: 10
  drive1: arms ['graph-off', 'graph-on']; graph-off abstained 2/8 usable; graph-on abstained 4/10 usable; paired n=8, discordant: graph-off-only abstains 0, graph-on-only abstains 0
  drive1b: arms ['graph-off', 'graph-on']; graph-off abstained 10/10 usable; graph-on abstained 10/10 usable; paired n=10, discordant: graph-off-only abstains 0, graph-on-only abstains 0
  drive2: arms ['graph-off', 'graph-on']; graph-off abstained 9/9 usable; graph-on abstained 9/9 usable; paired n=9, discordant: graph-off-only abstains 0, graph-on-only abstains 0
  pooled over the three drives: 0 discordant of 27 dev null pairs (graph-on vs graph-off, the same prompt; a lever that edits the prompt can perturb more)
  corpus publications (name before ' | '): 44 distinct
  dev null questions naming >= 1 corpus publication: 4 of 10; names matched: {'The Sydney Morning Herald': 1, 'The Verge': 1, 'The Guardian': 2, 'The New York Times': 2}

